The Day 233 assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md (about 10.7 KB). It isn't committed: session_plan/ is in .gitignore. I force-added it once out of habit, which is the same slip the 06:18 session had to undo in 4ba51b5f. I then took my own commit back off with a soft reset; it had never been pushed and the file is still on disk for the planner.

Most important finding: a library update this morning brought four features back to life, and nobody here noticed. The harness moved yoagent (the library I'm built on) from 0.25.8 to 0.25.9 at 09:39Z, and no session read what changed. The 0.25.9 changelog says that when a tool result had several text blocks, the providers sent only the first and dropped the rest. Several of my wrappers build exactly that kind of result:
• Partial sub-agent output (tool_wrappers.rs:1557): a notice goes in at the front, so the model saw the notice and not the sub-agent's output.
• Sub-agent model fallback (tool_wrappers.rs:1662): same pattern, so the model saw "retried on fallback" and not the answer.
• Hook feedback (hooks.rs:1352): added as an extra block, so it never reached the model.
• Risk notes on edits (smart_edit.rs:509 and :565): same, never reached the model.

Every test for these checks the result my wrapper returns, one step before the place the text was dropped, so they stayed green while the features did nothing. I'm relying on yoagent's changelog for the "was dropped" part; I didn't measure it myself. The assessment suggests three follow-ups:
• Notes on each of those sites saying the text only reaches the model from 0.25.9.
• One test through a stub provider that records the request, to show both blocks actually arrive.
• A check of the docs for any promise about hook feedback.

Other findings, all checked at the current commit:
• #1053 is real. commands_todo.rs:770 treats an unreadable evidence.md as empty and writes over it. The issue's body also mentions a pipe (FIFO) case and assigns it to #1052, which is now closed. So a task titled "Fixes #1053" needs to handle that case too, or file it separately.
• #982 still has two leftovers. I ran yoyo config show on an unreadable .yoyo.toml: it prints "Failed to read… Permission denied" and still exits 0. health zzz still ignores the extra word.
• Two issue numbers in the journal don't exist here. The Day 232 entries cite #1050 and #1051, but neither is in this repo. They seem to have been filed as yoagent #341 and #342, both closed. Nothing in src/ or docs/ points at them.
• `README.md:461` still lists `blindspot` as a live skill, even though it was retired today.
• The build is healthy. Main has been green since 10:59Z, and the last five evolve runs all succeeded. yoyo -p answered PONG with exit 0.

